C. Permitted local, internal, and public-fork use

Subject to these terms, you may download, clone, fork, copy, modify, adapt,
translate, compile, build, run, and create derivative works of Covered
Materials for your own personal use, for internal use within your
organization, or in a public fork, provided that the public fork complies with
this section.

You may create and maintain a public fork of Covered Materials, including a
fork containing your modifications, only if:

(a) the fork retains these terms unchanged, together with all copyright
notices and this notice;

(b) you do not change, replace, remove, supplement, or otherwise alter the
license terms applicable to Covered Materials or your modifications, and you
do not relicense Covered Materials under any other terms;

(c) the fork is clearly identified as an unofficial fork and is not presented
as an official VerseBox CE release; and

(d) the fork does not distribute or make available any built binaries,
packages, ROMs, installers, release artifacts, or other externally
distributable products, except as expressly permitted in Section D.

Private forks, local copies, and internal modifications are permitted for
personal or internal organizational use. A public fork that changes the
license terms, removes this notice, or relicenses the materials is outside the
permission granted here.

D. Prohibited distribution and other uses

Except for a public fork permitted under Section C, you may not distribute,
publish, publicly display, publicly perform, upload, post, mirror, archive
publicly, redistribute, sublicense, sell, rent, lease, lend, or otherwise make
Covered Materials or any modified version available to any third party,
whether commercial or non-commercial, without separate written permission from
the relevant rights holder. You may not distribute any unofficial binaries,
packages, ROMs, installers, release artifacts, or other externally
distributable products based on Covered Materials. Official distribution may
be made only by the project maintainers or through channels they expressly
authorize in writing.

You may not incorporate Covered Materials into another product or project
that is distributed or made available externally, except for a public fork
that complies with Section C. Automated access or collection for external
distribution, public availability of release artifacts, or AI/ML use
prohibited under this section is outside the permission, including scraping,
crawling, indexing, and extraction by scripts, services, or bots. Automated
access solely for permitted local, internal, or public-fork build and testing
is allowed.

You may not supply Covered Materials, in whole or in part, as input or
context to an artificial-intelligence or machine-learning system, including a
large language model. You may not use them to train, fine-tune, evaluate,
prompt, augment, or otherwise develop such a model. This includes using the
materials for retrieval-augmented generation, including them in training,
fine-tuning, or evaluation datasets, or using them to generate embeddings,
summaries, or derived training signals, directly or through an intermediary.

To the extent the law permits a rights holder to reserve text-and-data-mining
rights, those rights are expressly reserved. This reservation includes the
opt-out under Article 4 of Directive (EU) 2019/790 where applicable.

